        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "974835f7-45b0-5003-bc97-f4ed420eff5c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rosario Castellanos, Lucy Maud Montgomery, Jean-Claude Andro, Carlos Fuentes, Anne Shirley\n- Places: Mexico, Canada, Prince Edward Island, Avonlea\n- Works: Anne of Green Gables, Zone sacrée, Chant des aveugles, Christ des ténèbres, Road to Avonlea\n- Roles: Poet, author, novelist, translator\n\nFacts:\n- Lucy Maud Montgomery was a Canadian author born on November 30, 1874, who published as L.M. Montgomery.\n- In 1908, Lucy Maud Montgomery began her best-known novel series with Anne of Green Gables.\n- Rosario Castellanos Figueroa was a Mexican poet and author born on May 25, 1925.\n- Jean-Claude Andro pursued a career as a novelist and translator.\n- Jean-Claude Andro translated Zone sacrée and Chant des aveugles by Carlos Fuentes and Christ des ténèbres by Rosario Castellanos.\n- Avonlea is a fictional community on Prince Edward Island, Canada.\n- Avonlea is the setting of Lucy Maud Montgomery's Anne of Green Gables and its sequels, which follow Anne Shirley.\n- Avonlea is also the setting of the television series Road to Avonlea.\n- Rosario Castellanos died on August 7, 1974.\n- Lucy Maud Montgomery died on April 24, 1942.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
